@namespace Ben.Web.Website.Library.Kit
@page "/field-kit/join/{Token}"

@*
    Where a lead's QR code lands for somebody WITHOUT the app (item 252).

    With the app installed, the phone never shows this page: the site claims /field-kit/join/* for
    the app (AppleAppSiteAssociation), so the camera opens Field Kit, which asks to join. This page
    is for everybody else, and says the one useful thing — get the app, then scan again.

    It names nothing. The token is enough to ask to join, and a code photographed and posted
    somewhere would otherwise tell a stranger what the group is doing tonight and where. The app
    shows the name, to somebody signed in, standing there.

    "Scan again" rather than anything cleverer: Apple has no deferred deep linking, so an app
    installed from this page cannot know what was scanned before it existed (item 248 found the
    same, and printed a code to type; a launch lasts one night, so scanning twice is simpler).
*@

<PageTitle>Join the group's session</PageTitle>

<div class="container py-5" style="max-width:560px;">
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body py-5 text-center" id="field-kit-join">
            <h3 class="mb-3">Join the group's session</h3>
            <p class="text-secondary">
                This code opens Field Kit in the IsHaunted app for iPhone and iPad, ready to record
                with the group. If you aren't one of the people registered, the app asks the lead to
                let you in — you can record while you wait.
            </p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary mb-4" href="@($"ishaunted://field-kit/join/{Uri.EscapeDataString(Token)}")"
               id="field-kit-join-open">
                Open in the IsHaunted app
            </a>
            <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
                Don't have it? Get <strong>IsHaunted</strong> from the App Store, sign in, then scan
                the code again.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Token { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
